codex
The generator was built and verified, but it is **parked—not shippable**.

The paper’s client-server definition (Section 1.1) and polynomial algorithms (Section 5.2) required an honest Track B classification. The projective shortcut proved too easy: 19/21 oracle attempts solved it through `p=4049`. The harness returned `budget_bound`, with `p=8101` still available. Per contract, I neither rejected nor shipped it. [Paper PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1011.3701)

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1011.3701/gen_1011_3701.py)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1011.3701/README.md)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1011.3701/selftest_report.json)
- [Oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1011.3701/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Harness metadata](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1011.3701/.meta.json)

Results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- G4: 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses.
- Four attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference Hopcroft–Karp: 8/8 successes, as Track B requires.
- G9 remains failed/pending because the bare hard preset was solved 3/3.
- Hinted/placebo runs were not performed after the park verdict, and no evidence was fabricated.
- No `REJECTED.md` was written.
